 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Fragments of a youth, far relieved from\nThe burden of this earth's harsh tyranny,\nSits upon the very walls of Heaven,\nAnd by his own name is called. 'Tis written\nAs though some one saw him ere he began,\nIn the distant past, to speak; seeing\nThat these are traits he can trace with perfect\nClarity, and yet scarcely feel being\nAught but an illusive phantom unseen.\nPerchance - that thought might well be allowed to\nA human form - he might perceive between\nHis breath and the light: - The source thereof",
